  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "Neural interactions in the human frontal cortex dissociate reward and punishment learning (Combrisson et al., 2024): preprocessed SEEG high-gamma power, 16 patients (derivative)",
  "description": "Preprocessed stereotactic EEG (SEEG) high-gamma power (50-100 Hz) from 16 patients with pharmaco-resistant epilepsy performing a probabilistic instrumental learning task with reward and punishment conditions. Data cover 248 bipolar derivations in the anterior insula, dorsolateral prefrontal cortex, lateral orbitofrontal cortex and ventromedial prefrontal cortex, time-locked to outcome. The derivative release supports information-theoretic analyses showing dissociable reward and punishment subsystems in the human frontal cortex.",
  "methods_description": "Depth electrode iEEG was recorded with a Micromed system (512 or 1024 Hz) in patients undergoing presurgical evaluation. Bipolar grey-matter derivations were computed, and gamma power (50-100 Hz) was estimated by multitaper transform, downsampled to 256 Hz and smoothed. Patients performed a probabilistic instrumental learning task with reward and punishment pairs of abstract cues, and trial-wise prediction errors were derived from a Q-learning model.",
